  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Assisted Voluntary Return and Reintegration for Victims of Trafficking and Foreign Citizens in Prostitution in Sweden VII (AVRRTiPP VIII)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall objective of the programme is to contribute to the availability and further strengthening of safe and dignified assisted voluntary return (AVRR), as well as sustainable reintegration in countries of origin, for victims of trafficking and foreign citizens in prostitution or otherwise subject to exploitation in Sweden. Within this phase of the programme, the aim is to provide AVRR for a further 20 persons, with at least 80 potential beneficiaries informed of the programme. The programme will also continue to provide reintegration assistance to returnees from previous programme phases, an estimated 83 beneficiaries, in view of recovery and sustainable reintegration. All assistance will be tailored to meet the needs of the individual and will be guided by a victim-centred and rights-based approach, paying due attention to aspects such as age, ethnicity, and medical needs.</narrative>
  </description>
